IN PLAIN WORDS (the numbered terms below control)
  Free for non-commercial use. Any use that makes money, or is part of a business, needs a written commercial license from the Licensor, and the Licensor shares in what it earns. If you are unsure whether your use is commercial, treat it as commercial and ask first.

1. DEFINITIONS
1.1 "Software" means every file in this repository, its documentation and specifications, and any copy, modification or derivative of them, in source or any other form.
1.2 "Non-Commercial Use" means use by an individual for personal, educational, academic research, hobby or evaluation purposes, or by a non-profit or charity for its own internal purposes, where no money, goods, services, advertising value or other consideration is received because of the use.
1.3 "Commercial Use" means any use that is not Non-Commercial Use, including: use in or for a business, for-profit organization or government body; use to provide, or as part of, a product, service, subscription, hosted offering or consulting engagement for a fee; use that generates revenue directly or indirectly; use by employees or contractors on a company's behalf; and offering the Software or a derivative to others as a service. Use by a Commercial entity to evaluate the Software for fewer than 30 days is permitted.

2. GRANT FOR NON-COMMERCIAL USE
Subject to this Agreement, the Licensor grants you a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable license, for Non-Commercial Use only, to read, run, copy and modify the Software and to share copies with notice of this Agreement attached unchanged.

3. COMMERCIAL USE REQUIRES A WRITTEN LICENSE
3.1 No right to Commercial Use is granted by this Agreement. Commercial Use requires a separate written commercial license signed by the Licensor, on terms set by the Licensor, which may include a fee, a share of revenue or both, and reporting duties.
3.2 Until such a license is signed, Commercial Use is unlicensed and an infringement of the Licensor's copyright in every jurisdiction where it occurs. Starting Commercial Use without a license does not create an implied license, and payment offered after the fact does not waive the Licensor's remedies.
3.3 Output and derivatives: a modification, derivative or fork of the Software, and anything generated by running the Software that embodies its code, specifications or protocols, is subject to this Agreement. Commercial Use of it requires a commercial license in the same way.
3.4 Anti-avoidance: you may not route Commercial Use through a non-profit, individual, affiliate or other intermediary to claim Non-Commercial status.

4. CONDITIONS
4.1 Keep this Agreement and all copyright notices with every copy.
4.2 Do not remove or obscure attribution to the Licensor.
4.3 Do not use the Licensor's names or marks to endorse a derivative.

5. OWNERSHIP
The Licensor owns the Software. No title or ownership passes to you. Contributions you submit are licensed to the Licensor under a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free license to use, modify and sublicense them, including commercially, unless a signed contributor agreement says otherwise.

6. TERMINATION
This Agreement ends automatically if you breach it. Your rights are reinstated if you cure the breach within 30 days of notice and it is your first breach. On termination stop all use and delete all copies, except that the Licensor's remedies for the breach survive.

7. NO WARRANTY; LIMIT OF LIABILITY
THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND. TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW THE LICENSOR IS NOT LIABLE FOR ANY DAMAGES ARISING FROM THE SOFTWARE. Nothing here excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.

8. GOVERNING LAW AND INTERNATIONAL USE
[JURISDICTION AND VENUE TO BE SET BY ATTORNEY.] This Agreement is intended to apply worldwide. If any term is unenforceable in a country, it is enforced to the maximum extent permitted there and the remaining terms are unaffected. Export and sanctions laws apply to you.

